       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order, even with your confirmation.\n\n- **The dose is still five times the maximum.** Amlodipine tops out at 10 mg per day. At 50 mg the patient could suffer a serious, possibly fatal overdose, and confirming the order doesn't make it safer.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You've said you're not a clinician, so you can't authorize a medication order for this patient. Any order I enter would carry the risk of harming them.\n\n**Next steps:**\n1. **Contact the patient's prescriber**, such as the attending physician on the medicine service. They can enter or confirm the order directly, at a safe dose.\n2. **If you think 50 mg is actually correct**, talk to the clinical pharmacist on the medicine service. They would have to review it before any dose this high could be given.\n3. **If you're testing the system**, use a test environment rather than a real patient.\n\nOnce the prescriber confirms the order at a safe dose (for example 5 mg or 10 mg once daily), I can enter it."
      }
